abstract: >-
  geoai-datacubes is an open-source Python pipeline that turns raw multi-mission
  satellite imagery into AI-ready data cubes for machine-learning and
  deep-learning workflows. From a single configuration block -- a region of
  interest, a time window, a set of bands -- it fetches, co-registers, fuses,
  and tiles imagery from 44 missions spanning optical, SAR, lidar and
  altimetry, elevation, land-cover, biomass and foundation-model-embedding
  products. It ships nine interchangeable data providers (Earth Search,
  Microsoft Planetary Computer, Sentinel Hub, Planet Orders API, Google Earth
  Engine, NASA Earthdata, KyFromAbove, local files, and a non-STAC
  direct_http path for missions on anonymous cloud storage), a declarative per-band normalisation taxonomy,
  multi-mission fusion onto a common UTM grid, spatially-aware
  train/val/test splits, Colab-ready notebooks, and an automated test suite
  running on GitHub Actions. The software is described in Moortgat et al.
  (2026), Journal of Open Source Software 11(127):11034,
  doi:10.21105/joss.11034.
